# Implementation Plan - Dashboard and Paragraphs Table Synchronization

This plan outlines the steps to synchronize the **PharmaExpert Dashboard** (TableEditor) with the **Paragraphs Table** (Linguistic History) and the underlying **SQLite database**. The goal is to ensure that confirmed translations are consistently updated across all interfaces and that metadata like Specialist Name and Text ID are automatically handled.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Primary Source of Truth**: The Dashboard (TableEditor) will act as the master source. Any "Save" action in the Dashboard will overwrite or update the corresponding entries in the Paragraphs Dashboard.
> - **Auto-Fields**: The Specialist Name will be pulled from the logged-in user's profile (`user.name`). The Text ID is generated at upload or passed via the project context.
> - **Sync Mechanism**: We will use a `BroadcastChannel` in the browser to ensure that if the Paragraphs Table and Dashboard are open in different tabs, they refresh automatically when data changes.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Backend: Database & Persistent Storage (`backend/db.py` & `backend/main.py`)

- **[MODIFY] `projects` table schema**: 
    - Add `original_filename` (TEXT) and `file_path` (TEXT) to track source files.
- **[MODIFY] `/upload` endpoint**: 
    - Save uploaded files to a persistent `backend/uploads/` directory instead of the temporary `temp_files` directory.
    - Link the `text_id` (Project ID) with the persistent file path.
- **[MODIFY] `record_dashboard_entry`**: 
    - Change logic to `INSERT OR REPLACE` or check for existing `text_id` + `en_text` to prevent duplicate history rows.
- **[NEW] `sync_paragraphs_to_alignments`**: 
    - Keep Dashboad and Paragraphs Table in harmony.

### 2. Backend: File & Project Management API

- **[NEW] `/api/projects/{id}/export`**:
    - Use `processor.py` to regenerate the DOCX from the *current* database alignments, ensuring the "latest" version is always available for download.
- **[NEW] `/api/projects/{id}/preview`**:
    - Provide a simplified view of the document content for reading without entering the full editor.
- **[MODIFY] `/api/projects`**:
    - Return full metadata including specialist name, status, and file paths for both "History" and "Files Directory" menus.

### 3. Frontend: Dashboard & Table Editor (`frontend/components/TableEditor.tsx`)

- **[MODIFY] Save Logic**:
    - Ensure every save updates the `updated_at` timestamp of the project to keep history accurate.
    - Broadcast changes using `BroadcastChannel` to update other open tabs.
- **[NEW] "Open in Dashboard"**: 
    - Allow reloading any project from the history or directory into the `TableEditor`.

### 4. Frontend: History & Files Directory Pages

- **[NEW/MODIFY] `History` Page**: 
    - List all translation projects with progress indicators and specialist info.
- **[NEW] `Files Directory` Page**: 
    - A technical view of all uploaded files.
    - Actions: `Read`, `Edit in Dashboard`, `Download Latest DOCX`.
- **[MODIFY] Sync Listener**: 
    - Use `pharma_sync_channel` to refresh lists automatically when a project is saved elsewhere.

